LOGBOOK.md:13:### 2245 — Rekey/open deadline coverage uses the injected clock (BUG-260811-3qdo3e)
LOGBOOK.md:14:- ROOT CAUSE: Reviewer round 3 passed the accepted cancellation, keepalive, and pressure regressions but unfiltered run 3 exposed a final fixture race in `rekeyCoalescingAndOpenScheduling`. The test intentionally held rekey while a first channel open consumed a real 300 ms deadline, then gave a second expected-success open the same real deadline. Aggregate scheduler latency could expire that second open before the observer resumed rekey, so a scheduler delay—not the production contract—selected `.timedOut`.
LOGBOOK.md:15:- IMPLEMENTATION: The test now injects `ManualFixtureClock`, waits until the first queued open has registered its 300 ms timer, and advances exactly 300 ms to preserve the pre-admission timeout assertion. It then keeps the clock fixed while the second open queues and rekey resumes, removing wall-clock scheduling from the success boundary without extending a timeout, sleeping, skipping, or weakening the expected error.
LOGBOOK.md:16:- VERIFICATION: The exact rekey/open case passes after the change, and the five cancellation/rekey/automatic-keepalive/channel-pressure regressions pass together 30/30 consecutive focused runs. A fresh reset-on-any-failure streak passes 20/20 unfiltered `swift test --skip-build` runs with 427 tests in 35 suites per run and exit 0, including prior failure positions 3, 13, 16, and 17. `make validate-core`, `make validate-libssh2`, strict recursive Swift format lint, and `git diff --check` exit 0. The pre/post sshd listener set remains the same older PIDs 1330 and 34815, and TASK-260715-1u2vpc's approved algorithm matrix remains present.
LOGBOOK.md:19:- ROOT CAUSE: A fresh post-review aggregate gate reproduced one final in-scope test race at the historical run-13 position. `automaticKeepaliveSurvivesLongRekey` used at most 500 scheduler yields before reading each `keepalivesSent` counter. Under aggregate load, the automatic task had not emitted `.keepaliveSent` before either assertion, even though the fatal keepalive self-join was fixed and the suite exited normally. Fixed yield counts are not a synchronization boundary.
LOGBOOK.md:20:- IMPLEMENTATION: `SuspendingRekeyObserver` now counts production `.keepaliveSent` events and resumes continuation-backed threshold waiters. The positive long-rekey test awaits the first and second emitted events before asserting the corresponding transport counters. Manual-clock advancement, rekey suspension, scoped cancellation, no implicit idle timeout, fatal teardown ownership, and the TASK-260715-1u2vpc algorithm matrix are unchanged; no sleep, timeout, skip, or wall-clock mask was added.
LOGBOOK.md:21:- VERIFICATION: The four lifecycle regressions pass together 30/30 consecutive focused runs. A final reset-on-any-failure streak passes 20/20 unfiltered `swift test --skip-build` runs with 427 tests in 35 suites per run and 16–18 second durations, including historical runs 13, 16, and 17. `make validate-core`, `make validate-libssh2`, warning-free recursive Swift format lint, and `git diff --check` exit 0. The sshd listener set before and after remains the same older PIDs 1330 and 34815.
LOGBOOK.md:22:- ANOMALY: The first fresh streak reset at run 7 with an unrelated HEV association snapshot assertion; the exact HEV case immediately passed focused. The next streak reset at run 13 with the reproduced keepalive counter race above. Both failing exit-1 logs are retained and neither run was counted toward the final streak.
LOGBOOK.md:25:- REVIEW: The scoped cancellation test plus the positive and fatal automatic-keepalive regressions pass together with exit 0, and inspection accepts the no-self-join ownership fix, zero-resource assertions, and retained TASK-260715-1u2vpc algorithm matrix.
LOGBOOK.md:27:- FINDING: The pressure fixture waits only for the actor-side count to reach 64 while the admitted exit operations concurrently enter network progress and failure cleanup. A waiter can begin channel disposal before the above-cap probe is admitted, causing `beginChannelOperation` to prefer the disposal code `.cancelled` over the cap error. Rework must make the cap boundary deterministic without weakening the expected error, skipping the case, or masking it with timing.
LOGBOOK.md:30:- ROOT CAUSE: Independent run 16 passed the repaired caller-cancellation case, then hung in `automaticKeepaliveSurvivesLongRekey`. A socket failure or close race in the transport-owned keepalive entered `handleOperationFailure`, awaited fatal teardown, and teardown attempted to drain that same `automaticKeepaliveTask`. This self-join parked both the keepalive and `transport.close`; the injected `ManualFixtureClock` made teardown's otherwise bounded timer remain suspended and exposed the cycle deterministically. This supersedes the earlier assumption that only the cancellation fixture's two remote sleeps caused the aggregate hang.
LOGBOOK.md:31:- IMPLEMENTATION: Keepalive now follows the established automatic-rekey ownership rule. Public `sendKeepalive` callers still await fatal teardown, while the transport-owned automatic keepalive starts teardown without awaiting it, returns through its failure handler, and can then be drained by teardown. A real-sshd regression advances the manual clock into an automatic keepalive, injects a socket failure, and requires `.closed` plus a zero owned-resource snapshot; no sleep, skip, wall-clock timeout, security policy, or approved-algorithm change was introduced.
LOGBOOK.md:32:- VERIFICATION: The exact scoped-cancellation/no-idle-timeout case passes 30/30 focused runs; the positive long-rekey keepalive case, the new fatal-keepalive regression, and all 25 LibSSH integration cases pass. Twenty consecutive unfiltered `swift test --skip-build` runs each pass 427 tests in 35 suites with exit 0, including the prior run-13 and run-16 failure points. `make validate-core`, `make validate-libssh2`, recursive Swift format lint, and `git diff --check` exit 0. The before/after sshd listener set remains the same two older PIDs, 1330 and 34815; no validation-owned listener leaked. TASK-260715-1u2vpc's approved-algorithm matrix remains intact.
LOGBOOK.md:33:- ANOMALY: Two later exploratory streaks were discarded after isolated assertion failures: the unchanged `PacketFlowBridgeBoundedTests.reverseTimeBudget` observed fake-clock yield count 1 instead of 2 and immediately passed focused, and the pre-existing `concurrentSameChannelWrites` test allowed EOF to race a not-yet-admitted writer and received the contract-correct `writeAfterEOF`. Neither failure involved the repaired cancellation or automatic-keepalive cases. With no change to those out-of-scope tests, a fresh reset-on-any-failure gate then completed 20/20 consecutive 427-test runs on the final tree.
LOGBOOK.md:36:- ROOT CAUSE: The real-sshd cancellation test opened two `sleep 2` exec channels while injecting a `ManualFixtureClock`. Caller cancellation correctly detached the pending read, but the following channel disposal still had to advance libssh2 cleanup behind the bridge-owned POSIX service and remote process exit. Because the manual clock also owned the channel-close deadline and was no longer advanced, cleanup could not expire independently; suite completion depended on two wall-clock subprocess lifetimes and could hang when socket/sshd retirement lost the favorable scheduling race. A clean baseline measured 4.116 seconds for this test, matching the two sequential sleeps.
LOGBOOK.md:38:- VERIFICATION: The exact test passes 30/30 focused invocations and fell to 0.193–0.275 seconds in aggregate runs. The serialized 24-test real-sshd suite, recursive Swift format lint, `swift build`, `make check-libssh2`, and `make validate-libssh2` exit 0. Twenty consecutive unfiltered `swift test --skip-build` runs each pass all 426 tests with exit 0 and no new sshd listener. The pre-existing `TASK-260715-1u2vpc` approved-algorithm matrix remains intact.
LOGBOOK.md:39:- ANOMALY: Adding `Process.waitUntilExit()` after the fixture's existing `isRunning` polling produced a reproducible Foundation wait deadlock in an unrelated socket-failure case; a process sample captured the stack and the attempted change was fully reverted. The original bounded sshd stop logic remains unchanged.
LOGBOOK.md:43:- IMPLEMENTATION: Every connection close now participates in a lock-protected pending-teardown barrier. The barrier completes only after adapter bookkeeping and, for locally initiated closes, registry cleanup. All post-EOF adapter snapshot assertions in `HEVUDPDatagramAdapterTests` await this seam; the suite is serialized to keep its blocking socket fixtures from starving one another under full-suite load. No adapter cancellation or generation semantics changed, and no sleep, retry, eventually assertion, or wall-clock polling was added.
LOGBOOK.md:44:- VERIFICATION: Strict Swift format lint, `swift build`, the 12-test adapter suite, and twenty consecutive focused invocations of both named tests pass. Unfiltered `swift test` produced a maximum clean streak of 12 runs (426 tests each); run 13 hung after the adapter suite passed in 1.735 seconds, in the unrelated pre-existing `caller cancellation is scoped and idle reads have no implicit timeout` LibSSH integration test. The same external hang recurred in two earlier gate attempts; each interrupted run leaked one task-created sshd fixture, which was identified by its fresh task directory and terminated without touching older fixtures. The required 20 consecutive unfiltered-run claim remains blocked by that out-of-scope anomaly.
