LOGBOOK.md:582:- LIFECYCLE: Registry retirement cancels an incarnation-local context on close, idle expiry, generation replacement, session loss, process shutdown, or parent cancellation. Active and queued jobs recheck that context before resolver/socket work, and token-scoped socket admission prevents a paused old lookup from reopening or sending through a same-generation reused ID. Deterministic barriers restore job, queue, name, payload, result, completion, worker, association, timer, socket, and descriptor counts to their declared baselines.
LOGBOOK.md:589:- ARCHITECTURE: Resolution is synchronous on the caller for up to the configured timeout, while the concurrency test supplies its own goroutine. The relay I/O layer needs a bounded asynchronous resolver job/worker seam that reserves association ownership before lookup, invalidates completion by exact token, and returns all jobs and reservations to baseline on close, expiry, session loss, and cancellation.
