LOGBOOK.md:1006:- FINDING: Snapshot lifecycle is sticky-correct: `SSHConnectionStateMachine`'s own snapshot resets to nil on transition to `userAuthentication`/`active`, but `NIOSSHHandler` re-reads it after every processed message while the KEX state machine still holds `NegotiationResult`, and only overwrites on non-nil (`NIOSSHHandler.swift:684`). Consequence: during a rekey the handler snapshot updates when the new `NegotiationResult` is computed (KEXINIT processing), slightly before newKeys activate.
