codex
The existing harness already covers a macOS loopback OpenSSH server, both approved algorithm rows, rekey, direct TCP/IP, exec, and teardown. The missing piece is a task-owned, privacy-safe manifest/verifier that turns those ad hoc fixtures into an explicit matrix and records unavailable external rows honestly. I’m checking the exact prior readiness evidence and test seams before designing that layer.
