+- MATRIX: The task-scoped canonical manifest covers success, first use, changed host key, authentication rejection, channel rejection, early close, half-close, reset, server rekey, 75 ms latency, deterministic 10% connection loss, and disconnect. Direct-tcpip echo/sink/failure endpoints and the existing real-sshd algorithm/rekey harness are the reproduction seams; password, interactive auth, broad exposure, production data, and persistent root services remain prohibited.
+- VERIFICATION: The complete 26-test real-sshd libssh2 integration suite passes, including the new server-side unapproved-key rejection regression, primary/fallback algorithms, host-policy ordering, channel rejection, M0 flows, and rekey-safe traffic. Sixteen Python tests pass with 84.4% stdlib `trace` line coverage of the new tool. The full streamed 5 GiB source/sink reports exactly 5,368,709,120 bytes and `SHA256:fc01cfd7aebf90ff9491f8556131b6ef575c3e1fa33a0277ba28920bbaee7f54` without a payload file. Manifest validation, Python compilation, strict Swift format lint, JSON parsing, and `git diff --check` exit 0.
