+# TASK-260715-39xz9g — SSH matrix fixture handoff
+
+## Outcome
+
+The reproducible M0 fixture contract now covers current macOS, current Linux,
+the approved older compatibility profile, and the real relux host through
+non-root public-key identities. The canonical public manifest is
+`TASK-260715-39xz9g_ssh-matrix-fixture-manifest-v1.json`.
+
+| Server row | Observed environment | Access and host identity evidence |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| macOS current | macOS 26.5 arm64; OpenSSH 10.2p1 | Ephemeral loopback sshd, non-root current user, Ed25519 host/user keys; per-run public fingerprint recorded |
+| Approved older profile | macOS 26.5 arm64; OpenSSH 10.2p1 forced to group14-sha256/P-256/aes128-ctr/hmac-sha2-512 | Ephemeral loopback sshd, non-root current user, P-256 host/user keys; negotiation test passed |
+| Linux current | Ubuntu 24.04 aarch64; OpenSSH 9.6p1 | Task-named plain Lima VM with no project mounts, loopback SSH forward, non-root Ed25519 identity; three public host-key fingerprints captured pre-auth |
+| Real relux | Darwin x86_64; OpenSSH 9.9p2 | Owner-approved `ssh-config://relux` reference, host key captured before auth, strict pinned known-hosts BatchMode authentication, non-root Ed25519 identity |
+
+No hostname, IP address, username, key path, private key, secret value, or
+remote content is present in the committed or board artifacts. The real-host
+public fingerprints are Ed25519
+`SHA256:0rW8XQXvHoWyOSnIAFaCT3NJmFRJF8khYQGdoZnvycg`, ECDSA
+`SHA256:TLorKoiqGs1taG4Dyl2co80/DaahdKSs9Z2kJtyEVmg`, and RSA
+`SHA256:kKrHhGHo1ZSIck7qvp0POWPHUA2WLJNpvGCVIGpZHwc`.
+
+## Deterministic branches
+
+The manifest and executable tests cover success, host-key first use, host-key
+change, authentication rejection, channel rejection, early close, half-close,
+reset, server rekey, 75 ms latency, deterministic every-tenth-connection loss,
+and disconnect. Direct-tcpip echo/sink/failure endpoints are implemented in
+`scripts/ssh_matrix_fixture.py`; the existing loopback OpenSSH harness supplies
+real SSH auth, channel, algorithm, and rekey coverage. Password and interactive
+auth, broad exposure, production data, and persistent root services are denied.
+
+## Traffic evidence
+
+The source/sink pipe streamed exactly 5,368,709,120 bytes (5 GiB) with seed
+`TASK-260715-39xz9g`. The sink reported
+`SHA256:fc01cfd7aebf90ff9491f8556131b6ef575c3e1fa33a0277ba28920bbaee7f54`.
+No payload file was created or retained.
+
+## Validation
+
+- `make ssh-fixtures-test`: exit 0; 16/16 tests passed.
+- `swift test --filter LibSSH2AdapterIntegrationTests`: exit 0; 26/26 tests passed.
+- Full 5 GiB source-to-sink pipeline: exit 0 with exact byte count and hash.
+- Python stdlib `trace`: 84.4% line coverage for `scripts/ssh_matrix_fixture.py`.
+- Manifest verification, Python compilation, strict Swift format lint, JSON
+  parsing, and `git diff --check`: exit 0.
+- `task-board validate`: exit 0; it also printed the existing aggregate anomaly
+  that `STORY-260715-lkshfz` is stored as `backlog` while this child is in
+  `development`. No parent-scope mutation was made by this tester task.
+
+Task logs are under `.temp/TASK-260715-39xz9g/`; the relevant files are
+`make-ssh-fixtures-01.log`, `swift-libssh2-integration-01.log`,
+`python-coverage-02.log`, `traffic-5gib-01.log`, and `teardown-01.log`.
+
+## Teardown and rotation evidence
+
+The task-owned Lima VM was stopped and deleted. Ephemeral private host/user
+keys, hashed known-hosts files, and raw SSH diagnostics were purged from both
+the workspace and Trash. Post-teardown checks report:
+
+```text
+task_vm_present=0
+work_sensitive_files=0
+trash_sensitive_files=0
+task_owned_endpoint_threads=0
+retained_payload_files=0
+preexisting_sshd_pids=none
+```
+
+Reproduction generates fresh ephemeral local keys; rotation is teardown plus a
+new provision. Linux uses the Lima external identity store, and the real host
+uses the owner-managed SSH configuration reference. No task-owned secret is
+stored in git or board resources.
